# Investoyard mobile — API host
#
# COPY THIS TO `.env` BEFORE AN EAS BUILD. `.env` is gitignored (the root
# .gitignore blocks `.env` and `.env.*`, allow-listing `.env.example`), so a
# clean checkout has no API host at all — and `lib/api.ts` then falls back to
# the BUILD MACHINE's LAN IP from Expo's host URI, or to localhost. Either one
# produces an app that cannot reach anything once it is off that machine, and
# the failure looks like a dead API rather than a missing file.
#
# For a build anyone else will run, set it explicitly:
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://newipoapi.finwave.co/api

# Leave it UNSET for local development against a dev API: Expo derives the dev
# machine's LAN IP, so a physical phone in Expo Go on the same Wi-Fi reaches it
# automatically and a simulator falls back to localhost.
#
# The deployed host above is deliberate for day-to-day work — the phone then
# hits the SAME database as the web app, so an IPO entered once in admin is
# testable on both surfaces against one dataset. A real device reaches it
# through Cloudflare; only this sandbox's own IP is bot-blocked.
#
# NOTE the API did NOT move with the web domain: the site is investoyard.com,
# the API is still newipoapi.finwave.co, and the shipped mobile build is
# compiled against that host. Changing it means standing up a new API host
# ALONGSIDE this one, never instead of it.
